---
import HeroImage from '../../assets/project-zomboid-server-hero.png';
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

// Turnstile site key (public by design; the secret lives in the Worker).
const TURNSTILE_SITEKEY = '0x4AAAAAAF9DDEBz6_0wP2po';
const RUNBOOK = '/blog/project-zomboid-dedicated-server-ubuntu-26-04/';
---

<Layout
	title="Managed Project Zomboid Server for Your Group — Peculiar Engineer"
	description="A private Project Zomboid dedicated server for a small group, run like production: tested backups, crash restarts, updates you can roll back, and mods checked before they touch your world. First month free for early groups."
	kind="page"
	showDate={false}
	heroImage={HeroImage}
>
	<p class="lede">
		I wrote <a href={RUNBOOK}>the runbook</a> for running a Project Zomboid server on Ubuntu, tested it on
		three throwaway boxes, and found the parts that bite: a default heap that gets the server OOM-killed, a
		crash that systemd records as a success, a broken mod that hangs while systemd still reports the server
		as running, and an update you can't undo without the right snapshot. If you'd rather play than run that
		yourself, I'll run it for you.
	</p>

	<h2>What you get</h2>
	<div class="table-wrap"><table>
		<thead>
			<tr><th>Thing that goes wrong</th><th>What I run so it doesn't ruin your weekend</th></tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr><td>Server crashes</td><td>Restarted automatically, back up in a few minutes</td></tr>
			<tr><td>A mod hangs the server at load</td><td>Health check on the game port restarts it and alerts me; I pull the bad mod</td></tr>
			<tr><td>A game update breaks your world or your mods</td><td>Snapshot before every update; rollback to the old build and the old world</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Disk dies, or someone wrecks the base</td><td>Daily off-server backups, and I test a restore every month</td></tr>
			<tr><td>New mod list</td><td>I boot it on a throwaway server first and tell you what fails, before it touches your world</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Admin chores</td><td>Whitelist, passwords, settings, resets: ask, and I do it</td></tr>
		</tbody>
	</table></div>

	<h2>Who it's for</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Private groups of about 5 to 10 players, one world.</li>
		<li>Build 42, vanilla or modded (a Workshop collection is ideal).</li>
		<li>Server in the US (East). Fine for North America; laggy from far away.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Price</h2>
	<p>
		The first month is free for the first couple of groups. In exchange, I ask for honest feedback on what
		works and what doesn't. After that it's <strong>$40 a month</strong> per group, cancel any time. If you
		leave, you get your world save.
	</p>

	<h2>The honest small print</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			It's one person, not a 24/7 support desk. The automation restarts crashed or hung servers and takes
			backups at 3 a.m.; a broken mod or anything else still needs me, when I'm awake.
		</li>
		<li>
			The server setup is <a href={RUNBOOK}>the public runbook</a>. Nothing is hidden, and you can always take
			it and run it yourself.
		</li>
		<li>
			Not affiliated with or endorsed by The Indie Stone. "Project Zomboid" is used only to say which game the
			server runs.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="apply">Apply</h2>
	<p class="form-error" id="form-error" role="alert" hidden></p>

	<form class="apply" method="post" action="/api/zomboid-apply">
		<label>Your name <input name="name" required maxlength="100" autocomplete="name" /></label>
		<label>Email <input name="email" type="email" required maxlength="254" autocomplete="email" /></label>
		<label>Discord handle (optional) <input name="discord" maxlength="100" /></label>
		<label>
			Group size
			<select name="group_size" required>
				<option value="">Choose…</option>
				<option value="2-4">2 to 4</option>
				<option value="5-8">5 to 8</option>
				<option value="9-10">9 to 10</option>
				<option value="11+">11 or more</option>
			</select>
		</label>
		<label>
			Mods: Workshop collection link, or "vanilla"
			<textarea name="mods" required maxlength="2000" rows="3"></textarea>
		</label>
		<label>When you play, with time zone (optional) <input name="schedule" maxlength="300" placeholder="e.g. Fri–Sun evenings, US Central" /></label>
		<label>Where you host now (optional) <input name="hosting" maxlength="300" placeholder="e.g. a friend's PC, a game host" /></label>
		<label>
			Top three complaints about your current server (optional)
			<textarea name="pains" maxlength="2000" rows="4"></textarea>
		</label>
		<div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
			<label>Leave this empty <input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
		</div>
		<div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITEKEY} data-theme="dark"></div>
		<button type="submit">Apply</button>
		<p class="note">Your details are only used to reply to you; I don't share them. I reply by email within a couple of days.</p>
	</form>

	<script is:inline src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>
	<script is:inline>
		(function () {
			var messages = {
				captcha: 'The spam check did not pass. Please try again.',
				invalid: 'Something in the form was missing, too long, or not a valid email address. Please check it and send again.',
				server: 'Something broke on my side. Please try again in a few minutes.',
			};
			var code = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('error');
			var box = document.getElementById('form-error');
			if (code && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(messages, code) && box) {
				box.textContent = messages[code];
				box.hidden = false;
			}
		})();
	</script>
</Layout>

<style>
	.lede {
		font-size: 1.1em;
	}
	form.apply {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1em;
		margin: 1.5em 0 2em;
	}
	form.apply label {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.35em;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--sys-dim);
	}
	form.apply input,
	form.apply select,
	form.apply textarea {
		width: 100%;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		padding: 0.6em 0.7em;
		background: var(--sys-bg);
		color: var(--sys-text);
		border: 1px solid var(--sys-dim);
		border-radius: 4px;
		font: inherit;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: max(16px, 1em); /* under 16px, iOS Safari zooms on focus */
	}
	form.apply input:focus,
	form.apply select:focus,
	form.apply textarea:focus {
		outline: 2px solid var(--sys-fg);
		outline-offset: 1px;
	}
	form.apply button {
		justify-self: start;
		padding: 0.6em 1.6em;
		background: var(--sys-fg);
		color: var(--sys-bg);
		border: 0;
		border-radius: 4px;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	form.apply .note {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--sys-dim);
	}
	.hp {
		position: absolute;
		left: -10000px;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.form-error {
		padding: 0.8em 1em;
		border: 1px solid #ff5f56;
		color: #ff9f99;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
</style>
